{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal, due to its design and positioning, would result in an incongruous and uncharacteristic addition to the street scene, causing harm to its character and failing to comply with adopted Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character) and CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal would result in harm to the neighbouring living conditions at 26 Carlton Avenue through the reduction of the dwellings garden space. The proposal therefore fails to comply with adopted Local Plan Policy SC5 (Ensuring Suitable Internal and External Space).",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development, by reason of the position of the parking space, excessive crossover width and consequential lack of visibility splays, would be likely to lead to a situation prejudicial to highway safety (including vulnerable road users such as pedestrians including school children and cyclists) contrary to Policy EC2 (Developing a Sustainable Local Transport Network) of the Local Plan together with the adopted Residential Crossovers and Off-street Parking Policy and the London Plan policy T6. "
  ],
